title: NeveFirst
---
Neve: Shapers in my lanes. I thought you were expensive warning lights. #emotion:Amused
Taren: Only when we hit something. #emotion:Smug
Neve: The Choir's sealed the Gullet's chambers. Take out the singers and the membranes loosen. And don't lean on the walls. #emotion:Worried
Neve: I left a cache in the second chamber. Copper beacon, cracked casing. Tell it I sent you. #emotion:Playful
<<setFlag neve.cache>>
===
title: NeveRepeat
---
Neve: The cache is yours. My advice costs extra: brake before you turn. #emotion:Smug
===
title: NevePost
---
Neve: That key's humming. Either it works or it's very pleased with itself. #emotion:Curious
Neve: The old survey runs you into walls. Check Sela's chart before you follow the beacon. Tallow's still answering. #emotion:Determined
===
title: OdaFirst
---
Oda: Mind the paint. Everything we own is in this hauler, and most of it's strapped to the outside. #emotion:Amused
Oda: We've filed for the Nacre transfer. One harbour, one berth, one departure a cycle. Nobody's left behind if everyone leaves together. #emotion:Neutral
Taren: And if the berth has a bad day? #emotion:Curious
Oda: Then it's a very bad day for a lot of people at once. My mother says I'm morbid. #emotion:Worried
===
title: OdaRepeat
---
Oda: Next transfer window, we go. Everyone at Nacre goes. That's the whole point. #emotion:Neutral
===
title: OdaPost
---
Oda: They've moved the transfer window up. Twice. Nobody at Nacre will say why. #emotion:Worried
===
title: IloFirst
---
Ilo: Anchor Compact survey. You're not in trouble. You're in a chart. #emotion:Amused
Ilo: We're measuring which routes will still hold a year from now. Director Venn publishes every figure, even the shelter corridor's capacity. #emotion:Neutral
Ilo: Read that number twice. Then decide whether your household files for a berth. #emotion:Worried
Taren: And the households that don't fit the number? #emotion:Neutral
Ilo: They're in the footnotes. I didn't write the footnotes. #emotion:Worried
===
title: IloRepeat
---
Ilo: The notice is posted at every dock. The capacity line is the short one. #emotion:Neutral
===
title: IloPost
---
Ilo: You went out toward the Gullet, didn't you? Keep your own notes. Ours get revised. #emotion:Determined
===
title: NeveParcelOffer
---
Neve: Heading back down to Sorrel? Good. I'm holding something of theirs. #emotion:Neutral
Neve: One of the three missed deliveries. Coffee, socks, and a letter somebody wrote twice. #emotion:Amused
Taren: You kept it? #emotion:Curious
Neve: The courier wouldn't land near the drill, and I wasn't going to space it. Take it to whoever's still answering down there. #emotion:Determined
<<startQuest NeveParcel>>
===
title: NeveParcelReturn
---
Neve: Well? Did it arrive warm? #emotion:Curious
Taren: The coffee did. They sent a reply. #emotion:Neutral
Neve: "Received with thanks. Please stop sending socks." That's the nicest thing anyone's said to me all cycle. #emotion:Happy
Neve: Keep these. Charge cells I was saving for an emergency, and you two look like one. #emotion:Amused
<<setFlag neve.parcelAnswered>>
===
title: OdaBerthOffer
---
Oda: You know the dock office on the Decks? Orrin's? #emotion:Neutral
Oda: Our berth token for the Nacre transfer went to his desk for a stamp and never came back. Without it, we're cargo. #emotion:Worried
Oda: He likes you. Ask him for it before my mother marches over there herself. #emotion:Amused
<<startQuest OdaBerth>>
===
title: OdaBerthReturn
---
Taren: One berth token, stamped. Orrin says he's sorry. #emotion:Neutral
Oda: You read it. Everyone reads it. One harbour, one berth, our names on line nine hundred and four. #emotion:Neutral
Oda: Nine hundred households ahead of us, all through the same door. Somebody thought that was a good idea. #emotion:Worried
Taren: If that door jams, find me. #emotion:Determined
Oda: I'll hold you to that. Here, for your trouble. Mother insisted. #emotion:Tender
<<setFlag oda.tokenReturned>>
===
